  "details": "The standard for animation rigs in 3D modeling software involves the ability to create bones whose transform, scale, and rotation are driven by other bones. This allows a huge variety in animation and control of mesh deformation that doesn't exist with Unity's constraint system, which only allows you to drive translation with translation, rotation with rotation, and scale with scale.\n\nAn example, which simulates a bicep contracting by controlling the length of a helper bone, can be seen here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4ygnG9hf2cI\n\nWith VRC Constraints, there's an opportunity to bring more advanced rigging to VRChat in a performant fashion. Allowing avatar creators to map the scale of a bone axis to the relative rotation of another bone, for instance, would allow muscular deformation. This could be as simple as mapping from a source to a target range of values, or include curves. I can forsee the ability to partially or fully (and automatically) port Blender animation rigs to VRchat, depending on how far the devs took this.",
